# Global Systems First (ABSOLUTE — ALWAYS ON)

**Highest-priority engineering rule for this repo.** Applies to **every** file change, fix proposal, and refactor — not only skills, not only when the user repeats it.

The project owner must **not** have to re-explain this. Agents enforce it on **every turn** without being asked.

## Priority order (when rules conflict)

1. **This rule** + `.cursor/rules/no-bandaid-fixes.mdc` + `.cursor/rules/skill-global-rules.mdc`
2. Roadmap / phase gates / architecture skills (`Simulator`, layers, timeline, `AbilitySystem`)
3. Convenience, speed, “small local fix,” model-default shortcuts

If a proposed edit violates (1) to satisfy (3) → **do not implement** until redesigned or the owner approves a documented exception.

## Every edit must

1. **Use the existing global system** that owns the behavior (sim, director, `AbilitySystem`, commit slots, data definitions, overlay derived from slots — not parallel logic).
2. **Minimize heuristics** — no second state machines, no UI-only flags that commit path ignores, no cursor/preview/click paths that disagree.
3. **Extend the canonical path** — one truth pipeline; preview == execution where applicable.
4. **Prefer data** over `if ability.id == …` / per-unit branches.
5. **Remove** the obsolete path in the same change when replacing behavior.

## Heuristic (forbidden unless owner-approved exception)

A **heuristic** here means: behavior driven by a local shortcut that is **not** the same rule the rest of the feature uses — e.g. a flag only presentation reads, a special case only one skill uses, a fix that makes hover/click disagree with `commit_from_slots`.

**Default: zero new heuristics.** Fix the owner system instead.

## Mandatory: exception warning (no silent bypass)

If the **correct** fix requires **breaking, bypassing, or adding an exception to** a global system, you **must stop** and post this block **before any edit**:

```
## ⚠ Global system exception (approval required)

**Global rule / system affected:** (name the system + file/API, e.g. commit slots, AbilitySystem.can_use, timeline column rule)

**Why the global path is insufficient:** (one paragraph — root cause, not symptom)

**Proposed exception:** (exact behavior change — what would diverge from the global rule)

**Alternatives considered:** (at least one way to stay on the global system, even if harder)

**Is this acceptable?** (yes / no / suggest alternative)
```

- Do **not** implement the exception until the owner replies **yes** to that specific exception.
- Do **not** hide exceptions in changelog prose — use the block above.
- “User said fix it fast” is **not** approval.

## Every proposal / fix must state (brief)

In gate messages, plans, and changelogs for non-trivial edits:

- **Global system used:** (e.g. `_build_commit_slots_at_cell` → `commit_from_slots`)
- **Heuristics added:** `none` or list each (must be `none` unless exception approved)

## Canonical global systems (Honor & Iron — non-exhaustive)

| Domain | Global owner |
|--------|----------------|
| Planning commit / cursor / preview | `combat_planning_input.gd` slots → `CombatDirector.commit_from_slots` / `preview_commit_valid` |
| Ability legality / range / targeting | `AbilitySystem` + ability data |
| Turn resolution | `Simulator.simulate` — headless, no Nodes |
| Skills / economy | Timeline columns, AP/MP, `EffectData` — see `skill-global-rules.mdc` |
| Living sandbox / map VFX | `sandbox_map_system.md`, `EffectsSettings`, GPU shaders — see `living-sandbox-architect.mdc` |

When unsure which system owns a behavior → **read and extend that system**; do not add a presentation-only workaround.

